cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline or its published models, please cite it as below."
title: "int8-pruning-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that takes PyTorch models through structured pruning, int8
  quantization, Edge TPU compilation and evaluation, applied across several
  model families (detection, classification, vision-language, person Re-ID,
  lane segmentation) with measured Coral USB results. The pruning method is
  DepGraph (Fang et al. 2023), applied through torch_pruning; what this
  pipeline carries over is the Edge TPU evaluation protocol of Zouhdi et al.
  (DSD 2026), established on CIFAR-100 classification, extended to four
  further tasks.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jiaheguo521/int8-pruning-pipeline"
# Author order reflects contribution to THIS software: Guo built and leads the
# pipeline; Zouhdi's CIFAR-100 study is what the classification pipeline and the
# Edge TPU benchmark path were built on, which is why he is an author here and
# not only a citation (he is also the first author of the DSD 2026 entry below;
# cite that one for the CIFAR-100 study itself); Kłoda supervised the work, recommended
# its research direction, and is a co-author of that same DSD 2026 entry.
#
# NEITHER work proposes a pruning method. That is DepGraph, the second entry
# below. Full per-criterion attribution is in ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md#references.
authors:
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Jiahe
  - family-names: Zouhdi
    given-names: Mouad
  - family-names: Kłoda
    given-names: Tomasz
#
# Carried out at LAAS-CNRS, Toulouse, France. Kłoda is also a co-author of the
# DSD 2026 entry below.

# 1. The CIFAR-100 study whose Edge TPU evaluation protocol this pipeline
#    follows. Cite this when referring to that study rather than to this
#    pipeline. 2. The structured-pruning method every family here actually uses.
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Pruning of Deep Neural Networks for Real-Time Execution on Edge TPU"
    year: 2026
    collection-title: "29th Euromicro Conference on Digital System Design (DSD)"
    location:
      name: "Kraków, Poland"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zouhdi
        given-names: Mouad
      - family-names: Guo
        given-names: Jiahe
      - family-names: Hammadi
